  "notes": [
    "Retain actual enum declarations, constructors, constants and value names; generated public const aliases preserve private references across generated libraries.",
    "Use resolved enum constructor elements to rename private constructor selectors, including enhanced generic declarations.",
    "A pinned CFE patch decodes only valid source-linker names in marked generated libraries inside synthesized _enumToString. Custom and inherited toString, super dispatch, user name getters and EnumName keep native semantics.",
    "Native display probes verify valid generated names, unmarked libraries and malformed encodings. Original-source AOT is a separate oracle.",
    "Enum value additions/removals/reordering and constructor arguments relink dependent classes, storage and typed functions; Enum-typed AOT consumers stay retained.",
    "Enum classes are excluded from the extendable contract. Original source privacy, invalid type arguments, forbidden inheritance/construction/mutable fields remain rejected; metadata is still rejected.",
    "The initial analyzer lookup call used the old positional API; corrected to the pinned named-parameter API before successful generation.",
    "The initial private enum constructor selector was not resolved on its identifier and failed Kernel compilation; it now uses the constant constructorElement and native regression passes.",
    "Applying the entire extended patch set to already-patched sources was refused as partial application. Only the new patch was applied after git apply --check; exact patch-set verification and the provenance-preserving host rebuild then passed.",
    "An early display override prototype was replaced before freezing by the frontend synthesis patch, retaining native custom/mixin/super behavior.",
    "Historical full native suite was not rerun; this report covers twenty-two rebuilt groups."
